          "Considers latency, throughput, cost, and failure modes."
        ],
        "4": [
          "Leads design for complex, multi-service systems; conducts effective design reviews.",
          "Introduces observability, resilience, and migration strategies."
        ],
        "5": [
          "Defines architectural vision; simplifies systems and reduces long-term cost.",
          "Influences platform roadmaps and standards."
        ]
      },
      "evidence_examples": [
        "Design docs and ADRs",
        "Capacity planning and cost analyses",
        "Post-implementation metrics (latency, error rates)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Collaboration and Communication",
      "description": "Works effectively with teammates and stakeholders; communicates clearly in writing and verbally.",
      "weight": 0.10,
      "behaviors_by_level": {
        "1": [
          "Communication is unclear or unresponsive; creates rework.",
          "Struggles to collaborate; conflicts remain unresolved."
        ],
        "2": [
          "Shares updates but misses key stakeholders or details.",
          "Requires facilitation to collaborate across functions."
        ],
        "3": [
          "Communicates timely and clearly; effective async updates.",
          "Contributes constructively to reviews and meetings."
        ],
        "4": [
          "Facilitates alignment across teams; reduces ambiguity.",
          "Coaches others on effective communication."
        ],
        "5": [
          "Trusted cross-org collaborator; influences without authority.",
          "Sets standards for documentation and knowledge sharing."
        ]
      },
      "evidence_examples": [
        "Status updates, RFC comments, meeting notes",
        "Stakeholder feedback",
        "Knowledge base contributions"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Ownership and Accountability",
      "description": "Takes responsibility for outcomes, including operational excellence and on-call duties.",
      "weight": 0.10,
      "behaviors_by_level": {
        "1": [
          "Avoids responsibility; issues recur due to lack of follow-through."
        ],
        "2": [
          "Handles assigned tasks but lacks end-to-end thinking."
        ],
        "3": [
          "Owns features/services through the lifecycle; addresses root causes.",
          "Participates responsibly in on-call and incident processes."
        ],
        "4": [
          "Leads incident response; drives postmortems and preventative actions.",
          "Improves SLIs/SLOs and reduces operational toil."
        ],
        "5": [
          "Builds a culture of ownership; establishes reliability practices across teams.",
          "Measurable improvements in availability and MTTR org-wide."
        ]
      },
      "evidence_examples": [
        "Incident timelines, postmortems, action item completion",
        "SLO attainment and reliability metrics",
        "Runbooks and automation"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Growth Mindset and Learning",
      "description": "Seeks feedback, learns new skills, and helps others grow.",
      "weight": 0.05,
      "behaviors_by_level": {
        "1": [
          "Resistant to feedback; minimal skill development."
        ],
        "2": [
          "Accepts feedback but applies it inconsistently."
        ],
        "3": [
          "Regularly incorporates feedback; learns relevant tools/tech quickly.",
          "Shares knowledge through pairing or docs."
        ],
        "4": [
          "Proactively identifies skill gaps; mentors and sponsors others.",
          "Drives internal learning sessions or guilds."
        ],
        "5": [
          "Cultivates a learning culture; builds programs with measurable skill uplift.",
          "Recognized for thought leadership."
        ]
      },
      "evidence_examples": [
        "Feedback loops and improvement actions",
        "Mentorship activities",
        "Training content and talks"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "calculation": {
    "method": "Weighted average of competency ratings using defined weights.",
    "example": {
      "ratings_input_example": {
        "Technical_Excellence": 4,
        "Execution_and_Delivery": 3,
        "Code_Quality_and_Maintainability": 4,
        "System_Design_and_Architecture": 3,
        "Collaboration_and_Communication": 4,
        "Ownership_and_Accountability": 3,
        "Growth_Mindset_and_Learning": 4
      },
      "weighted_average_formula": "sum(rating_competency * weight_competency)",
      "result_scale_mapping": {
        "1.0-1.9": "Does not meet expectations",
        "2.0-2.9": "Partially meets expectations",
        "3.0-3.6": "Meets expectations",
        "3.7-4.4": "Exceeds expectations",
        "4.5-5.0": "Outstanding"
      }
    }
  },
  "goals_section": {
    "short_term_goals": "3-6 months; specific, measurable, attainable, relevant, time-bound (SMART).",
    "long_term_goals": "6-18 months; career development, scope growth, and technical depth.",
    "examples": [
      "Increase service p95 latency improvement by 20% within two quarters.",
      "Lead design and delivery of feature X impacting Y customers by Q3.",
      "Mentor two junior engineers through onboarding and first project delivery."
    ]
  },
  "career_level_expectations": {
    "IC1_IC2": "Focus on skill building, task execution, and learning team practices.",
    "IC3": "Own medium features, contribute to designs, and maintain quality independently.",
    "IC4": "Lead complex projects, influence design, mentor others, and improve systems.",
    "IC5_plus": "Set technical direction across teams, drive org-wide impact, and raise the engineering bar."
  },
  "review_artifacts_checklist": [
    "Self-review with evidence links",
    "Manager review with specific examples",
    "Peer feedback (at least 3 peers across functions)",
    "Customer or stakeholder feedback (when applicable)",
    "Metrics dashboard links (reliability, performance, delivery)",
    "Key PRs, design docs, ADRs, and incident reports"
  ],
  "bias_mitigation_guidelines": [
    "Assess outcomes and evidence, not personality or style preferences.",
    "Use consistent criteria and the rating scale across all engineers.",
    "Account for scope, opportunity, and systemic factors.",
    "Avoid recency bias by reviewing full period data.",
    "Calibrate with other managers to ensure fairness."
  ],
  "final_recommendation_fields": [
    "overall_rating",
    "summary_of_strengths",
    "summary_of_opportunities",
    "promotion_consideration",
    "compensation_recommendation",
    "development_plan",
    "risk_and_retention_notes"
  ],
  "metadata": {
    "review_period": "e.g., 2025 H1",
    "reviewer": "Manager Name",
    "reviewee": "Engineer Name",
    "team": "Team/Org",
    "date_completed": "YYYY-MM-DD"
  }
}
